# Build context exclusions for image builds that use the repository root as
# their context — docker/build-container.sh (llama-swap.Containerfile) and
# docker/vllm-swap.Dockerfile.
#
# NOT used by docker/unified/build-image.sh: that one builds with
# docker/unified/ as its context, and Docker reads .dockerignore from the
# context root, so this file never applies there.
#
# The rule for adding a line here: the path must be generated output or local
# clutter that no Dockerfile in this repository copies. Everything a build
# reads from the context has to stay — docs/config.example.yaml, for one, is
# copied by llama-swap.Containerfile.

# Dependencies and build output. node_modules alone is ~218 MB of the ~226 MB
# context; the UI is built inside the image from a clean npm ci, never from a
# local install that may not match package-lock.json.
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
build/
dist/

# Generated by `make ui` and embedded into the binary at compile time (go:embed
# behind the embed_ui tag). It is produced inside the image, so shipping a
# stale local copy would only invite confusion.
internal/server/ui_dist/

# Version control. No Dockerfile here stamps a version from context git
# metadata — docker/vllm-swap.Dockerfile derives it from the clone it makes
# itself, and llama-swap.Containerfile takes it as a build arg. Remove this
# line if a future build needs `git describe` against the context.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Test and tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
evals/docs-agent/runs/
evals/config.yaml

# Local environment and editor state
.env
.env.*
.dev/
.aider*
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.DS_Store

# Local databases and logs produced by running llama-swap from the checkout
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log
